  "notes": [
    "Prototype contract; not an operational national yield model.",
    "Assortment sorts are dimension-only; no official BC grade is assigned.",
    "BTC grade shares are context only.",
    "Fail-closed on unexpected git deletions.",
    "Weibull-containing mixtures are fitted on the left-truncated grouped support; new-family unstable fits are reported but not selected, while the legacy two-gamma fallback may remain selected and is flagged.",
    "Spike families are attempted only when the first DBH bin exceeds the documented share or the best simple fit leaves a high KS. The spike carries the first bin and the continuous tail starts at the first bin upper edge; the spike weight is an AIC parameter and does not set the volume scale. Unconstrained spike tails are eligible only on the finite fitted support and are never extrapolated. Constrained spike tails use a bounded grouped MLE (shape >= 1, scale >= 0.1 cm); a fit at any bound is reported as boundary_reject and is not selected."
  ],
